<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Omnia sells Carnia Seeds to Cargill SA.</title>
<headline>Omnia sells Carnia Seeds to Cargill SA.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Omnia Holdings Ltd said on Monday that it had sold its seeds business Carnia Seeds to Cargill South Africa for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The firm said full details of the deal would be revealed when it publishes its year results on March 19. It added that the sale would have no material impact on its earnings and a beneficial effect on its balance sheet.</p>
<p>The cash garnered from the sale of Carnia will be used to develop the group's core businesses of fertilisers, explosives and industrial chemicals, the firm said.</p>
<p>Those three divisions made up 95 percent of Omnia's 1995 turnover of 834 million rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
